I started my journey as a professional artist, in 2023, after my mom passed away (she had cancer for almost 8 years prior and I was on hospice care, that led to a significant gap in my career), although academically I'm a molecular biologist that completed their post grand from NUST in 2020; I switched to pursuing art as my full time profession. I always wanted to go to art school but wasn't able to, (and looking at the state of art schools now, I'm low key glad I didn't.) 

I started off with traditional medium, painting canvases and murals, for commercial spaces. I then started learning and experimenting with digital medium with @procreate as my tool of choice, teaching myself illustration and animation. I'm super proud of the work I'm done in just 3 short years, working with some amazing people along the way such as 
